type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "cot⁡y+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337182} {:answer/id #uuid "cbbba5ec-56d3-5218-abf9-36a5e07211a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-cot⁡y+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337821}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7eef5879-dbe7-5b97-97a6-26e4a74a9d5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "cot⁡y+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337182} :answer-field/id #uuid "709f437f-6931-5254-8a8a-e5df59c326ec" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338469}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "e6d46060-4d10-5e18-98aa-e065865069a6" :question/math-academy-id "q-71664" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int -{csc}^{2}⁡y\\,\\text{d}y=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that \n\n$$\n\\int {csc}^{2}⁡y\\,\\text{d}y=-cot⁡y+C\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int -{csc}^{2}⁡y\\,\\text{d}y & =-\\int {csc}^{2}⁡y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =-(-cot⁡y)+C \\\\  & =cot⁡y+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338972 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1034906a-3ff2-5190-aa84-370c8a694595" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "cos⁡x+5cot⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336183} {:answer/id #uuid "1c0f4398-2a00-57b0-b576-0d1d9a1b08b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-cos⁡x+5cot⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336295} {:answer/id #uuid "51bee0d5-412a-55a2-aa71-c32c51cf3aef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-cos⁡x-5cot⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336781} {:answer/id #uuid "5355af50-9329-57b3-b77f-0f36a4e5d909" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-csc+5tan⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336801} {:answer/id #uuid "607d955e-a572-5487-a0b1-e0d64b2e6b4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "csc-5tan⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336905}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1c0f4398-2a00-57b0-b576-0d1d9a1b08b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-cos⁡x+5cot⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336295} :answer-field/id #uuid "7bafaa70-1f4e-59fb-9e5a-6775a181aa39" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338493}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "19dfcc66-7eec-5ed4-8474-81621b4b91ab" :question/math-academy-id "q-71666" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int sin⁡x-5{csc}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int sin⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =-cos⁡x+C, \\\\ \\int {csc}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =-cot⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int sin⁡x-5{csc}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int sin⁡x\\,\\text{d}x-5\\int {csc}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-cos⁡x-5(-cot⁡x)+C \\\\  & =-cos⁡x+5cot⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186344992 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0aa3632a-36d9-5d45-aada-3fed83e6dce0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342326} {:answer/id #uuid "653b4691-0f44-5149-acb3-ba490ce5be44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343095} {:answer/id #uuid "beffe86d-8d35-5522-bff5-c1bacb25479e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343916} {:answer/id #uuid "cb4cf03e-744a-54e5-90b3-81ce5dcd317d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{DNE}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344026} {:answer/id #uuid "cd9286e2-fe14-5bfe-9359-f7ac47372d45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344051}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0aa3632a-36d9-5d45-aada-3fed83e6dce0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342326} :answer-field/id #uuid "445577e8-8f70-5d8d-a39d-41e0418a56ad" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344605}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "a32523f7-b65a-5ea6-ad9b-ea76193dc862" :question/math-academy-id "q-74909" :question/problem "Find $\\lim_{x\\to (1,2)}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4-x-y).$" :question/worked-solution "Let the function $f(x,y)$ be defined as\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4-x-y).\n$$\n\nThe function $f(x,y)$ is continuous except when $4-x-y$  is negative or zero. However, at the point $(1,2)$,  the expression  $4-x-y$ is positive, so we can calculate the limit by substituting  $(1,2)$ into the function: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lim_{x\\to (1,2)}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4-x-y)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4-1-2)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1)=0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186344993 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "52b7df89-d99c-5b42-9cc2-063604231fef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342929} {:answer/id #uuid "8e43633a-b13b-5b08-9991-4a855a976614" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{DNE}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343484} {:answer/id #uuid "be0eb3e2-b2bb-5b4d-8e0b-d09e4ab2c128" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343913} {:answer/id #uuid "cd8ebb93-6c86-56d6-af46-1bb108780271" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344050} {:answer/id #uuid "d7a1e3df-1ed6-57d4-81e0-257ba2a81c67" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344132}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "52b7df89-d99c-5b42-9cc2-063604231fef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342929} :answer-field/id #uuid "a81e50a8-3dec-549b-a0cf-3a09d9dfb58b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344787}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "3f277d23-3dcb-54b8-9f1f-cefa2a015d92" :question/math-academy-id "q-74912" :question/problem "Find $\\lim_{x\\to (-2,4)}\\sqrt[3]{xy}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let the function $f(x,y)$ be defined as\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\sqrt[3]{xy}.\n$$\n\nThe function $f(x,y)$ is continuous for all values of $x$ and $y.$ So,  we can calculate the limit by substituting  $(-2,4)$ into the function: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lim_{x\\to (-2,4)}\\sqrt[3]{xy}=\\sqrt{(-2)\\cdot 4}=\\sqrt[3]{-8}=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186344994 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "154cde04-acab-5465-9547-10829d1c2ac6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342426} {:answer/id #uuid "6bb42284-ebac-5722-a55a-f3d61f6c5806" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343155} {:answer/id #uuid "92dfc28e-190d-569d-937c-6a93104fd226" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343523} {:answer/id #uuid "b4342938-2831-524c-937b-68dbdb102e85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343816} {:answer/id #uuid "dcaa824e-6288-5d0e-ba41-9737c9cd645c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344174}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "154cde04-acab-5465-9547-10829d1c2ac6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342426} :answer-field/id #uuid "0e203f08-9966-5d66-bfae-16443836045d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344522}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "267b24cc-56d4-5780-90e2-1ea13cc5ba4e" :question/math-academy-id "q-74918" :question/problem "Find  $\\lim_{x\\to (1,1,2)}\\frac{x{z}^{2}-y{z}^{2}}{yz-xz}.$" :question/worked-solution "Attempting to evaluate the limit by direct substitution leads to the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0},$ as follows: \n\n$$\n\\lim_{x\\to (1,1,2)}\\frac{x{z}^{2}-y{z}^{2}}{yz-xz}=\\frac{1\\cdot {2}^{2}-1\\cdot {2}^{2}}{1\\cdot 2-1\\cdot 2}=\\frac{0}{0}\n$$\n\nHowever, we can simplify the limit by canceling common factors in the numerator and denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lim_{x\\to (1,1,2)}\\frac{x{z}^{2}-y{z}^{2}}{yz-xz} & =\\lim_{x\\to (1,1,2)}\\frac{(x-y){z}^{2}}{(y-x)z} \\\\  & =\\lim_{x\\to (1,1,2)}-\\frac{(x-y){z}^{2}}{(x-y)z} \\\\  & =\\lim_{x\\to (1,1,2)}(-z)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the limit has been simplified, we can evaluate it using direct substitution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lim_{x\\to (1,1,2)}(-z) & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the limit evaluates to $-2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345000 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "23e684a3-31e7-5afb-abe6-889eedabcb7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342537} {:answer/id #uuid "428a1d63-be06-5a77-98e9-2febf282827f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342789} {:answer/id #uuid "49075012-2ea9-548d-9ca7-add606c5a0d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{DNE}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342838} {:answer/id #uuid "6d62d708-9b60-5aa8-8bc8-d437253c8433" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343176} {:answer/id #uuid "9a659bec-94b4-5e6e-bfad-430d6af2dd3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343597}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6d62d708-9b60-5aa8-8bc8-d437253c8433" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343176} :answer-field/id #uuid "68b1ada5-9d1d-5909-9bba-0575aa292e27" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344672}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "985d9983-0c2e-5408-a2e7-d78f48fa4c2a" :question/math-academy-id "q-74952" :question/problem "Find  $\\lim_{x\\to (-1,1)}\\frac{{x}^{2}+2xy+{y}^{2}}{{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}}.$" :question/worked-solution "Attempting to evaluate the limit by direct substitution leads to the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0},$ as follows: \n\n$$\n\\lim_{x\\to (-1,1)}\\frac{{x}^{2}+2xy+{y}^{2}}{{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}}=\\frac{(-1)^{2}+2\\cdot (-1)\\cdot 1+{1}^{2}}{{1}^{2}-(-1)^{2}}=\\frac{0}{0}\n$$\n\nHowever, we can simplify the limit by canceling common factors in the numerator and denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lim_{x\\to (-1,1)}\\frac{{x}^{2}+2xy+{y}^{2}}{{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}} & =\\lim_{x\\to (-1,1)}\\frac{(x+y)^{2}}{(y-x)(y+x)} \\\\  & =\\lim_{x\\to (-1,1)}\\frac{(x+y)(x+y)}{(y-x)(x+y)} \\\\  & =\\lim_{x\\to (-1,1)}\\frac{x+y}{y-x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the limit has been simplified, we can evaluate it using direct substitution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lim_{x\\to (-1,1)}\\frac{x+y}{y-x} & =\\frac{(-1)+1}{1-(-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{0}{2} \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the limit evaluates to $0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345001 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5a374dad-4f6b-524a-aa54-86b138bf78f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342993} {:answer/id #uuid "63a029bd-31fb-55ab-850e-9758cb89df9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343081} {:answer/id #uuid "8849f804-0c8c-53f5-8a8d-500546d52a81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343419} {:answer/id #uuid "8a9051dc-e91b-5b6b-8909-a2310cbbc28e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343442} {:answer/id #uuid "bd9e25dd-2c46-5b76-99a3-260d2e1e558e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{DNE}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343907}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "63a029bd-31fb-55ab-850e-9758cb89df9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343081} :answer-field/id #uuid "b313de74-d195-5d45-bc88-f2346a3b2f91" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344807}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "774103b5-b3b5-52ef-9d71-0bba2999450c" :question/math-academy-id "q-74957" :question/problem "$$\n\\lim_{x\\to (3,1)}\\frac{\\sqrt{x}-\\sqrt{y+2}}{x-y-2}=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Attempting to evaluate the limit by direct substitution leads to the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0},$ as follows: \n\n$$\n\\lim_{x\\to (3,1)}\\frac{\\sqrt{x}-\\sqrt{y+2}}{x-y-2}=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}-\\sqrt{1+2}}{3-1-2}=\\frac{0}{0}\n$$\n\nHowever, we can simplify the limit by first multiplying the numerator and denominator by the conjugate of the numerator: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lim_{x\\to (3,1)}\\frac{\\sqrt{x}-\\sqrt{y+2}}{x-y-2} & =\\lim_{x\\to (3,1)}\\frac{(\\sqrt{x}-\\sqrt{y+2})(\\sqrt{x}+\\sqrt{y+2})}{(x-y-2)(\\sqrt{x}+\\sqrt{y+2})} \\\\  & =\\lim_{x\\to (3,1)}\\frac{(\\sqrt{x})^{2}-(\\sqrt{y+2})^{2}}{(x-y-2)(\\sqrt{x}+\\sqrt{y+2})} \\\\  & =\\lim_{x\\to (3,1)}\\frac{x-y-2}{(x-y-2)(\\sqrt{x}+\\sqrt{y+2})} \\\\  & =\\lim_{x\\to (3,1)}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}+\\sqrt{y+2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow that the limit has been simplified, we can evaluate it:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lim_{x\\to (3,1)}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}+\\sqrt{y+2}} & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}+\\sqrt{1+2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}+\\sqrt{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the limit evaluates to $\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{3}}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345002 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "24eddf01-84ca-55d1-a380-e9e3dc0ff46c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342549} {:answer/id #uuid "46dbb611-211c-5a6d-87c1-e6d11b78516f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342824} {:answer/id #uuid "5b00ef31-06ca-5784-b242-7ba648259786" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342998} {:answer/id #uuid "5f565846-c8fc-53fd-9002-a2c55e2b4a8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343042} {:answer/id #uuid "740303a6-c0b7-5dc3-b4d8-e1c846a9c24f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343243}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5f565846-c8fc-53fd-9002-a2c55e2b4a8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343042} :answer-field/id #uuid "e02b8a03-215d-5182-84e4-5ebedc1e9c9a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344885}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "324536b7-fcd9-5a5e-87fe-4723a8ba3a5d" :question/math-academy-id "q-74958" :question/problem "$$\n\\lim_{x\\to (1,1)}\\frac{\\sqrt{x}-y}{x-{y}^{2}}=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Attempting to evaluate the limit by direct substitution leads to the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0},$ as follows: \n\n$$\n\\lim_{x\\to (1,1)}\\frac{\\sqrt{x}-y}{x-{y}^{2}}=\\frac{\\sqrt{1}-1}{1-{1}^{2}}=\\frac{0}{0}\n$$\n\nHowever, we can simplify the limit by first multiplying the numerator and denominator by the conjugate of the numerator: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lim_{x\\to (1,1)}\\frac{\\sqrt{x}-y}{x-{y}^{2}} & =\\lim_{x\\to (1,1)}\\frac{(\\sqrt{x}-y)(\\sqrt{x}+y)}{(x-{y}^{2})(\\sqrt{x}+y)} \\\\  & =\\lim_{x\\to (1,1)}\\frac{(\\sqrt{x})^{2}-{y}^{2}}{(x-{y}^{2})(\\sqrt{x}+y)} \\\\  & =\\lim_{x\\to (1,1)}\\frac{x-{y}^{2}}{(x-{y}^{2})(\\sqrt{x}+y)} \\\\  & =\\lim_{x\\to (1,1)}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}+y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow that the limit has been simplified, we can evaluate it:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lim_{x\\to (1,1)}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}+y} & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1}+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the limit evaluates to $\\frac{1}{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345003 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5225a54e-55a7-5758-ada6-d6e76ec121f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342920} {:answer/id #uuid "6afe5058-ed29-5490-84ca-cf5ea037f221" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343150} {:answer/id #uuid "72810408-6a46-5e8d-9beb-52bbe2e8f436" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343231} {:answer/id #uuid "c186d6e7-0ac4-5259-897c-07e60f6cc561" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343939} {:answer/id #uuid "fd70e6c7-52f3-50c1-9a16-a6b4b41da448" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344465}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6afe5058-ed29-5490-84ca-cf5ea037f221" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343150} :answer-field/id #uuid "c5121edc-c04d-5ea2-9e7a-1a1ca983765e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344836}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "580ed3de-301a-5585-aa08-af0b5b637cec" :question/math-academy-id "q-74960" :question/problem "$\\lim_{x\\to (1,1)}\\frac{{y}^{2}-x}{\\sqrt{x}-y}=$" :question/worked-solution "Attempting to evaluate the limit by direct substitution leads to the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0},$ as follows: \n\n$$\n\\lim_{x\\to (1,1)}\\frac{{y}^{2}-x}{\\sqrt{x}-y}=\\frac{{1}^{2}-1}{\\sqrt{1}-1}=\\frac{0}{0}\n$$\n\nHowever, we can simplify the limit by first multiplying the numerator and denominator by the conjugate of the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lim_{x\\to (1,1)}\\frac{{y}^{2}-x}{\\sqrt{x}-y} & =\\lim_{x\\to (1,1)}\\frac{({y}^{2}-x)(\\sqrt{x}+y)}{(\\sqrt{x}-y)(\\sqrt{x}+y)} \\\\  & =\\lim_{x\\to (1,1)}\\frac{({y}^{2}-x)(\\sqrt{x}+y)}{{(\\sqrt{x})}^{2}-{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\lim_{x\\to (1,1)}\\frac{-(x-{y}^{2})(\\sqrt{x}+y)}{x-{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\lim_{x\\to (1,1)}-(\\sqrt{x}+y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the limit has been simplified, we can evaluate it:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lim_{x\\to (1,1)}-(\\sqrt{x}+y) & =-(\\sqrt{1}+1) \\\\  & =-(1+1) \\\\  & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the limit evaluates to $-2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345004 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "83f3e9a8-09a1-5f57-86fa-04e7b6915e56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468094} {:answer/id #uuid "78fcd3c1-4a11-58fd-8ce6-df88fc49f25d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468095}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "78fcd3c1-4a11-58fd-8ce6-df88fc49f25d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468095} :answer-field/id #uuid "2c6cf87b-5ae8-56c1-a044-0835a6c8cde4" :answer-field/key "The limit evaluates to $0$ along the path $y=x$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468768} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "311f4a3b-6073-5441-be15-0e0c7cc774ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468096} {:answer/id #uuid "88d6ad28-2d86-517c-95bc-f86d6c74568c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468097}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "88d6ad28-2d86-517c-95bc-f86d6c74568c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468097} :answer-field/id #uuid "d491b47c-a016-53fb-a14f-bea3b0d37235" :answer-field/key "The limit evaluates to $2$ along the path $y={x}^{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468769} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b5f46b92-20fa-5e06-82d5-4d57f3b2567e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468098} {:answer/id #uuid "5c70d63f-3608-5e38-a9a1-5aca4eef4730" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468099}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b5f46b92-20fa-5e06-82d5-4d57f3b2567e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468098} :answer-field/id #uuid "a0d14fb0-548c-5014-9418-0de578d5c27b" :answer-field/key "The limit exists and is equal to $2$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468770}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "d5fe00a2-ab56-5281-b3c2-6fe8dad2417a" :question/math-academy-id "q-74964" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the limit given below?\n\n$$\n\\lim_{x\\to (0,0)}\\,\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{2{x}^{2}-y}\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Attempting to evaluate the limit by direct substitution leads to the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0}:$\n\n$$\n\\lim_{x\\to (0,0)}\\,\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{2{x}^{2}-y}=\\frac{2\\cdot {0}^{2}}{2\\cdot {0}^{2}-0}=\\frac{0}{0}\n$$\n\nHowever, the function cannot be simplified by canceling common factors in the numerator and denominator:\n\nWe attempt to evaluate the limit by approaching $(0,0)$ from different paths.\n\n- Statement “The limit evaluates to $0$ along the path $y=x$” is true. Taking $x\\to (0,0)$ along the path $y=x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lim_{x\\to (0,0)\\,\\,\\,y=x}\\,\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{2{x}^{2}-y} & =\\lim_{x\\to 0}\\,\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{2{x}^{2}-x} \\\\  & =\\lim_{x\\to 0}\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{x(2x-1)} \\\\  & =\\lim_{x\\to 0}\\frac{2x}{2x-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot 0}{2\\cdot 0-1} \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “The limit evaluates to $2$ along the path $y={x}^{2}$” is also true. Taking $x\\to (0,0)$ along the path $y={x}^{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lim_{x\\to (0,0)\\,\\,\\,y={x}^{2}}\\,\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{2{x}^{2}-y} & =\\lim_{x\\to 0}\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{2{x}^{2}-{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\lim_{x\\to 0}\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\lim_{x\\to 0}\\,2 \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “The limit exists and is equal to $2$” is false. Because the limit evaluates to different results on two different paths, we conclude that the limit does not exist:\n\n$$\n\\lim_{x\\to (0,0)}\\,\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{2{x}^{2}-y}=\\text{DNE}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345005 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3baf4567-d424-573a-9e30-4ff96fa2d669" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342729} {:answer/id #uuid "4f893e89-6a93-53ab-b746-44f7cf20c423" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342900} {:answer/id #uuid "6f5dd490-0f0f-53bd-b098-70c3ce3d0f06" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343196} {:answer/id #uuid "9c9e3fe9-3652-5268-9ac3-a883593c3468" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343618} {:answer/id #uuid "a0f15882-a4eb-5654-8f46-170a82fde8d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{DNE}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343658}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a0f15882-a4eb-5654-8f46-170a82fde8d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{DNE}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343658} :answer-field/id #uuid "e7ab88d0-e46a-5e99-86e7-68aecdee4f07" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344896}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "56c07c72-df51-5ec4-88ac-9185b7690371" :question/math-academy-id "q-74966" :question/problem "$\\lim_{x\\to (0,0)}\\,\\frac{2y{x}^{3}}{{x}^{6}+8{y}^{2}}=$" :question/worked-solution "Attempting to evaluate the limit by direct substitution leads to the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0}:$\n\n$$\n\\lim_{x\\to (0,0)}\\,\\frac{2y{x}^{3}}{{x}^{6}+8{y}^{2}}=\\frac{2\\cdot 0\\cdot {0}^{3}}{{0}^{6}+8\\cdot {0}^{2}}=\\frac{0}{0}\n$$\n\nHowever, the function cannot be simplified by canceling common factors in the numerator and denominator:\n\nLet's attempt to evaluate the limit approaching $(0,0)$ from different paths.\n\n- Taking $x\\to (0,0)$ along the path $y=x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lim_{x\\to (0,0)\\,\\,\\,y=x}\\,\\frac{2y{x}^{3}}{{x}^{6}+8{y}^{2}} & =\\lim_{x\\to 0}\\,\\frac{2{x}^{4}}{{x}^{6}+8{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\lim_{x\\to 0}\\,\\frac{2{x}^{4}}{{x}^{2}({x}^{4}+8)} \\\\  & =\\lim_{x\\to 0}\\,\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{{x}^{4}+8} \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Taking $x\\to (0,0)$ along the path $y={x}^{3},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lim_{x\\to (0,0)\\,\\,\\,y={x}^{3}}\\,\\frac{2y{x}^{3}}{{x}^{6}+8{y}^{2}} & =\\lim_{x\\to 0}\\,\\frac{2{x}^{6}}{{x}^{6}+8{x}^{6}} \\\\  & =\\lim_{x\\to 0}\\,\\frac{2{x}^{6}}{9{x}^{6}} \\\\  & =\\lim_{x\\to 0}\\,\\frac{2}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBecause the limit evaluates to different results on two different paths, we conclude that the limit does not exist:\n\n$$\n\\lim_{x\\to (0,0)}\\,\\frac{2y{x}^{3}}{{x}^{6}+8{y}^{2}}=\\text{DNE}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348396 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "188951c5-b647-59de-87db-4f6c6b426d9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/c4/c4f19e6b424610387a8973b037c3f4636c09dba441ab1d6bd36dbe103d779a88.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345567} {:answer/id #uuid "a08f9159-c1f0-5d9d-9faa-036322f0f4ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/77/770f3089576cabd68f3c80b597eb4f15df279538c49853526b0ea123bc75af08.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346754} {:answer/id #uuid "a91b1c88-e8a7-5b29-af5d-037d5dd16059" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/82/8255d8370e49983ff0e37b5068a8a997de5eeadaedf7bd7869cf5dcd3c826ca1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346823} {:answer/id #uuid "b930def4-6682-5174-b08b-663fd943ac8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/e1/e1ca6081e8077bcbc54de6a71e10ef1d278bbbc6b99842f1eee0d3dfcb71ebda.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346959} {:answer/id #uuid "e88b14e0-794c-5f33-8cc8-2732ab08b857" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/5b/5b77994fcd8b675c439a37e1b2049c0c6d266f12b3dc298b3183133b9010c818.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347401}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b930def4-6682-5174-b08b-663fd943ac8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/e1/e1ca6081e8077bcbc54de6a71e10ef1d278bbbc6b99842f1eee0d3dfcb71ebda.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346959} :answer-field/id #uuid "7fb0239c-d4e5-5a09-af6a-e5c0ec1b636b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347830}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "a57b32c5-cfbb-5d77-9ba0-fa861f47a6d6" :question/math-academy-id "q-80499" :question/problem "Which of the following diagrams gives the slope field at the points indicated for the differential equation $$\n\\displaystyle \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{x+2y}{4}?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We have to sketch the slope field at the points $(4,-2),(2,1),$ and $(-1,3).$\n\nTo sketch the slope field at the given points, we substitute their coordinates into the right-hand side of the differential equation.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(4,-2)}=\\frac{4+2(-2)}{4}=0, \\\\  & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(2,1)}=\\frac{2+2(1)}{4}=1, \\\\  & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(-1,3)}=\\frac{-1+2(3)}{4}=\\frac{5}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting up our points and drawing our line segments, we get the following diagram.\n\n![](images/e1/e1ca6081e8077bcbc54de6a71e10ef1d278bbbc6b99842f1eee0d3dfcb71ebda.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360821 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "95bf5c87-5d3a-5cc2-9253-891ef7730177" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438628} {:answer/id #uuid "3d5d5215-469a-5799-ba24-eb8bc4c358d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438629}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "95bf5c87-5d3a-5cc2-9253-891ef7730177" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438628} :answer-field/id #uuid "f545d324-f9c3-507e-983b-fd1001340ff1" :answer-field/key "At every point in the first quadrant, the slope of the slope field is positive" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439343} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "33b8f3b3-189f-5b75-9ccc-ddd834e75d7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438630} {:answer/id #uuid "d83106e2-c95a-541f-8d33-b2ba054c50ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438631}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d83106e2-c95a-541f-8d33-b2ba054c50ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438631} :answer-field/id #uuid "e7dbe69a-f051-5886-8cde-e2c1753c8657" :answer-field/key "At every point in the second quadrant, the slope of the slope field is positive" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439344} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e25dae65-1d55-511a-b24e-a8cb350771d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438632} {:answer/id #uuid "41b3f2e3-0dfd-5365-982e-fd4103306c05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438633}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e25dae65-1d55-511a-b24e-a8cb350771d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438632} :answer-field/id #uuid "d8887387-6555-5bd2-8c67-a09c271d9b0f" :answer-field/key "At every point in the fourth quadrant, the slope of the slope field is negative" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439345} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dd1c2bdc-0469-523c-91f6-c855085c7da3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668743} {:answer/id #uuid "51177707-2eb7-5aed-a139-336e31875353" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668744}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dd1c2bdc-0469-523c-91f6-c855085c7da3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668743} :answer-field/id #uuid "df2afb4d-c42b-5d56-a228-5938eaf763e0" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668949}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "9ebbc31b-8f74-56d3-8d4f-392a8aeeda85" :question/math-academy-id "q-97477" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-xy$ and its slope field. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, we define $f(x,y)=-xy.$ Then, our differential equation is $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x,y).$ \n\nNotice that $f(x,y)=0$ when $x=0$ or $y=0.$ The lines $x=0$ and $y=0$ divide the plane into the usual four quadrants.\n\nIf we compute the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each quadrant (by considering some test points, for example), we get the following:\n\n![](images/2c/2c218c7df2bf4e159b4bffaccb4296beab8e3f44ab82d56b3589050af92ccf8e.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement “At every point in the first quadrant, the slope of the slope field is positive” is false. If $(x,y)$ is in the first quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)<0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is negative for any point $(x,y)$ in the first quadrant.\n\n- Statement “At every point in the second quadrant, the slope of the slope field is positive” is true. If $(x,y)$ is in the second quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in the second quadrant.\n\n- Statement “At every point in the fourth quadrant, the slope of the slope field is negative” is false. If $(x,y)$ is in the fourth quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in the fourth quadrant."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360822 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "af5c066d-bd1b-5916-a240-8a09350060cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438634} {:answer/id #uuid "e033cbd9-4a9c-558a-b84e-515ba29c5965" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438635}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "af5c066d-bd1b-5916-a240-8a09350060cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438634} :answer-field/id #uuid "86f3af7d-b3a9-5b53-9913-e3d5d3053834" :answer-field/key "At every point in the first quadrant, the slope of the slope field is negative" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439346} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "adc85b15-3131-50c7-b7d4-2e649a9fb136" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438636} {:answer/id #uuid "409eb813-3391-5d94-b0e1-4012a919fc2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438637}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "409eb813-3391-5d94-b0e1-4012a919fc2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438637} :answer-field/id #uuid "cdc4db1c-cf09-591b-bae6-192098ed008b" :answer-field/key "At every point in the second quadrant, the slope of the slope field is negative" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439347} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e92256da-0966-5c42-98d2-bb15e2c0f12d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438638} {:answer/id #uuid "eea8981c-85f6-57b9-bcd6-78db1679f73c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438639}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e92256da-0966-5c42-98d2-bb15e2c0f12d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438638} :answer-field/id #uuid "cdfcbe44-29db-570c-9bd7-2b09381a9273" :answer-field/key "At every point in the fourth quadrant, the slope of the slope field is positive" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439348}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "4ffe3a0e-6b8b-5f1d-8f45-5dd040381266" :question/math-academy-id "q-97482" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=9xy$ and its slope field. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, we define $f(x,y)=9xy.$ Then, our differential equation is $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x,y).$ \n\nNotice that $f(x,y)=0$ when $x=0$ or $y=0.$ The lines $x=0$ and $y=0$ divide the plane into the usual four quadrants.\n\nIf we compute the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each quadrant (by considering some test points, for example), we get the following:\n\n![](images/6e/6ef852c9c15dc6f591119906abe479949f929edb6dc26f21588b4de545d02da2.png)\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement:\n\n- Statement “At every point in the first quadrant, the slope of the slope field is negative” is false. If $(x,y)$ is in the first quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)>0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is positive for any point $(x,y)$ in the first quadrant.\n\n- Statement “At every point in the second quadrant, the slope of the slope field is negative” is true. If $(x,y)$ is in the second quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)<0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is negative for any point $(x,y)$ in the second quadrant.\n\n- Statement “At every point in the fourth quadrant, the slope of the slope field is positive” is false. If $(x,y)$ is in the fourth quadrant, then according to our diagram, we have\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(x,y)}=f(x,y)<0.\n$$\n\nThis implies that the slope of the slope field is negative for any point $(x,y)$ in the fourth quadrant."}]}
